<https://id.i2idl.org/concepts/xapi-extension> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://id.i2idl.org/concepts/xapi-statement> <https://id.i2idl.org/graphs/concepts/xapi-extension/versions/1> .
<https://id.i2idl.org/concepts/xapi-extension> <https://glossarystudio.app/ns/activeDefinition> <https://id.i2idl.org/definitions/xapi-extension-1> <https://id.i2idl.org/graphs/concepts/xapi-extension/versions/1> .
<https://id.i2idl.org/concepts/xapi-extension> <https://glossarystudio.app/ns/editorialExplanation> "Extensions give communities room to represent domain-specific information while keeping the core Statement model stable; interoperability is strongest when built-in properties are used whenever possible." <https://id.i2idl.org/graphs/concepts/xapi-extension/versions/1> .
